### 10. Testing Strategy

#### 10.1 Testing Levels

**Unit Testing (UTC):**
- **Scope**: Individual methods and classes in isolation
- **Backend**: Test service methods, repository queries, utility functions using JUnit 5 and Mockito
- **Frontend**: Test Vue components, composables, utility functions using Vitest
- **Target Coverage**: Minimum 70% for critical business logic (services, controllers)
- **Execution**: Run automatically on each commit via CI/CD (if set up) or manually before integration

**Integration Testing (ITC):**
- **Scope**: Test interactions between components (Controller → Service → Repository → Database)
- **Backend**: Test REST API endpoints with real database (test database), verify data persistence and retrieval
- **Frontend-Backend**: Test API calls from frontend to backend, verify request/response formats
- **External Services**: Test Qwen AI integration, email service integration (mock or test environment)
- **Execution**: Run after each feature completion, document results in Test Plan

**System Testing (STC):**
- **Scope**: End-to-end testing of complete user workflows
- **Test Scenarios**:
  - User registration → login → create post → view in feed → receive AI moderation result
  - Daily briefing crawl → AI summarization → user search → view detail → open original link
  - User A follows User B → send message → mark as read → delete conversation
  - Profile update → language switch → verify UI language change
- **Execution**: Run before each milestone, document in Test Record

#### 10.2 Test Environment

- **Development Environment**: Local machine with test database
- **Test Database**: Separate MySQL instance with test data (reset before each test run)
- **Mock Services**: Mock Qwen AI responses for unit tests (use real API for integration tests)
- **Test Data**: Predefined test users, posts, comments, messages for consistent testing

#### 10.3 Test Documentation

- All test cases documented in `BridgeU-TestPlan.md` with:
  - Test case ID, description, preconditions, steps, expected results
  - Test execution records with pass/fail status, actual results, defects found
- Traceability: Each test case linked to requirements via `BridgeU-TraceabilityRecord.md`

